/* G-3.4: the Info.plist half. `INFOPLIST_KEY_*` in the pbxproj bakes a literal into the generated
   Info.plist, which is a user-visible string with no catalogue behind it — this file is what makes
   it translatable. The build setting stays as the development-language value; this overrides it per
   locale, and a new .lproj here is all another language needs.

   TR-1.9 / FR-1.8.2: the sentence in the Health permission sheet. It names what is read and says
   where it goes (G-5.4), because the system prompt names the app and the data type and nothing
   else. */
"NSHealthShareUsageDescription" = "TotalCraft reads your body mass from Health so your weigh-ins and their seven-day average are in one place. Imported readings are kept with the rest of your log.";

/* G-5.4: the app never writes to Health (`requestAuthorization(toShare: [], …)`), so this sheet is
   never shown. The key exists because App Store Connect refuses an upload whose HealthKit
   entitlement lacks it (validation error 90683), and the text has to stay true if it is ever read. */
"NSHealthUpdateUsageDescription" = "TotalCraft never writes to Health. Your weigh-ins and training log stay in the app, and this permission is never requested.";
